[14.397629, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[53.305544, "o", "Done. All three deliverables are in place and verified.\r\n\r\n**Filter used**\r\n```jq\r\nmap(select(.status == \"active\"))\r\n| map({\r\n    user_id: .id,\r\n    username: .username,\r\n    email: .email,\r\n    last_login: (.last_login | sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")),\r\n    role_count: (.roles | length),\r\n    primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)\r\n  })\r\n| sort_by(.username)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Files**\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` — 346 active users, 2-space indented, sorted by `username` ascending.\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh` — the exact executed command: `jq --indent 2 '<filter>' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`.\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml` — `filter` (single-quoted YAML scalar so `\\.` survives) plus `args: [\"--indent 2\"]`.\r\n\r\n**Verification**\r\n- Rebuilding via `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml) /app/users.json` produced byte-identical output (`diff` clean).\r\n- Output user_id set equals exactly the `status == \"active\"` id set (346 of 500; 98 inacti"]
[53.305767, "o", "ve, 56 pending excluded).\r\n- All `last_login` values match `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`; all usernames are in sorted order.\r\n- 50 users have empty `roles` and yield JSON `null` for `primary_role`; no mismatches between `role_count == 0` and null `primary_role`.\r\n\r\nOne note on the date parsing: jq 1.6's `fromdateiso8601` rejects fractional seconds, so the filter strips `.<fraction>Z` → `Z` before parsing, converting through `strftime` rather than truncating the string.\r\n"]
